## Overview

Fixes #65934. With `--tool-call-parser olmo3`, streaming dropped any assistant text that starts with `<` but is not a tool call (for example `<p>hello`). The response came back as HTTP 200 with empty content, while non-streaming returned the text. This PR holds text back only while it can still become `<function_calls>`, and releases it once that is ruled out. Real `<function_calls>` output streams as before, including when the tag is split across tokens, and non-streaming is unchanged.



## Validation

